Z||000016||Ken Wittlief||06-18-2001||10:24 AM||||To misquote the movie Jaws:<P>"Were gonna need a bigger extinquisher!"<P>  I heard before that once they get going the plastic body panels burn like a demon - by the time the firetruck gets there, they all look like this.<P>  This may be a little morbid, but can you post the first photo again with less jpg compression? can you post it at like 99% quality?<P>  or was the photo itself blurry like that.<P>  I am not critizing your photography skills - Id like to get the best possible copy of that image.<P>  BTW - I congradulate you for having a camera in your car for what I hope will be a once in a lifetime photo op!<P>  it reminds me - when I moved to Iowa from PA many years ago, on the way out we passed the burned out hulk of a tractor trailer in the median of I90 - it looked like a giant skeleton, like in the days of the wagon trains when you would come across the skeletons of someones Ox team in the middle of the trail:<P>  "This is a bad omen! - Martha! wheres my Hawkin rifle?"<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
