Z||000020||DJRice||06-18-2001||12:22 PM||||Its not really a desolate area, as that is on US1 outside the West Entry Gate of Kennedy Space Center.  Unfortunately, It is about 2 miles to the closest fire station.  <P>When I passed the car on the way home, we were undergoing an unbeliveable rain storm, so I went to my apartment, grabbed the digital camera, and headed back to the scene.  I can redownload the pic on a different setting and see if it gets any better but the camera is only a 320x240.  <BR>(I am currently digital camera shopping, as its definitely time to upgrade)<BR>Maybe I'll swing by there again today and see if the carcass is still there and take a regular photo to scan.<P>Now, for the EBay ad:<P>This 1984 Fiero is a true collectible.  It is one of only a handful remaining that did not have the recall work performed.  A little TLC and this car will be as good as new.  Needs Engine, transmission, complete electrical system, seats, dashboard, carpet, gauge kit, quarter panels, roof, fenders, door skins & glass, tires, brakes discs, calipers, and pads, belts, hoses, A/C compressor, spare tire, windshield washer motor, windshield wipers, windshield, headlight motors, & radiator.  <P>Would be excellent for that Ferrari Kit youve been thinking about.  Dont miss this opportunity, bid today!<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Tigger||06-18-2001||01:04 PM||||If it's still there, can you take a closer look to check to see if it has the added heat shields etc. around the exhaust manifolds, they should have been added if it had recall work done to it.  Who knows, it just might have a big gaping hole in the block.<P>I know it's pretty crispy and pretty hard to tell, just would like to know or try to determine the cause of death for this one.<P>it's just aweful   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
