Z||000038||FieroJoe||06-18-2001||10:54 PM||||My dad, who is a firefighter of many years, remebers putting out a few 84 fires before the recall.  Though where we live is out of his departement's jurisdiction, he had heard on his scanner that there was a Fiero on fire just down the road from where we live.  He got there just about the time the firefigthers were, and said that the car went up in bright flames as soon as the body panels caught, and that there was magnesium wheels on the car, and that when the water hit them they just burnt even hotter.  Apparantly, whatever coating is on mag wheels to keep them from burning when it rains had burned off from the heat, so raw magnesium was exposed.<P>||||reg||1
